From: Banana <bananalinux@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 28 Oct 2026 18:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gfx/vulkan: draw the OSD and widgets with the panel's turn

The menu is a software texture blitted with mvp_menu (patch 0010), but everything
else the driver draws for the interface -- the notifications, the FPS counter, the
volume widget -- comes out sideways. It reaches vulkan_draw's `draw` entry two
ways: gfx_display_draw_quad passes no matrix at all (the driver fell back to
mvp_no_rot), and gfx_widgets' icon helper passes rot(get_default_mvp). On KMS/GBM
nothing above RetroArch turns the output, so both answers have to be the turned
matrix -- mvp_menu, the one the menu texture is blitted with. (ROCKNIX never needs
this: RetroArch runs windowed under sway, which turns the output.)

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/gfx/drivers/vulkan.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers/vulkan.c
@@ -1269,7 +1269,10 @@
    vk_t *vk = (vk_t*)data;
    if (!vk)
       return NULL;
-   return &vk->mvp_no_rot;
+   /* The widgets' icons are drawn as rot(get_default_mvp); hand it the turned matrix or they stay in
+    * the framebuffer's portrait orientation while the menu is upright (see mvp_menu in
+    * vulkan_set_projection). */
+   return &vk->mvp_menu;
 }
 
 static const float *gfx_display_vk_get_default_vertices(void)
@@ -1477,7 +1480,7 @@
                ? vk->samplers.linear
                : vk->samplers.nearest);
             call.uniform      = draw->matrix_data
-               ? draw->matrix_data : &vk->mvp_no_rot;
+               ? draw->matrix_data : &vk->mvp_menu;
             call.uniform_size = sizeof(math_matrix_4x4);
             call.vbo          = &range;
             call.vertices     = draw->coords->vertices;
